  "vignette": "A 58-year-old man is brought to the emergency department because of 3 days of fever, headache, watery diarrhea, and a cough productive of scant sputum. Symptoms began 5 days after he returned from a 4-day convention at a large hotel. He has smoked one pack of cigarettes daily for 30 years. On examination he is confused about the date. There are crackles over the right lower lung field. Vital signs and laboratory studies are shown.",
