  "vignette": "A 24-year-old man is brought to the emergency department 30 minutes after a head-on motor vehicle collision in which he was the unrestrained driver. He complains of diffuse abdominal pain. His airway is patent and breath sounds are equal bilaterally. The abdomen is distended and diffusely tender. Vital signs, laboratory studies, and bedside imaging findings are shown. After 1 L of warmed crystalloid and initiation of a blood transfusion, blood pressure is 88/60 mm Hg and pulse is 122/min.",
