  "vignette": "A 23-year-old man is admitted after sustaining a closed midshaft tibial fracture in a soccer game; the leg is placed in a long posterior splint. Ten hours later he reports steadily worsening leg pain that is not relieved by repeated doses of intravenous morphine. The splint and all circumferential dressings are removed. The anterior leg is tense and markedly swollen, passive movement of the toes produces severe pain, and sensation is decreased in the first dorsal web space. The dorsalis pedis and posterior tibial pulses are 2+ bilaterally. Vital signs and laboratory studies are shown.",
